---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const post = {
 title: 'Custom Embroidered T-Shirts: When They\'re the Right Choice',
 description:
 'Compare embroidered t-shirts with screen-printed tees. Review exact products, artwork, placement, decoration compatibility, care, availability, pricing, and current order terms.',
 category: 'Products',
 readTime: '7 min read',
 date: 'May 9, 2026',
 isoDate: '2026-05-09',
 image: '/images/generated/service-embroidery.jpg',
 slug: 'custom-embroidered-t-shirts-buyer-guide',
}

const faqs = [
 { q: 'Can you embroider on a t-shirt?', a: 'Many t-shirts may support embroidery. Compatibility depends on the exact fabric, construction, artwork, placement, digitizing, backing, use, and care. The production partner must approve the exact garment and design.' },
 { q: 'Should I embroider or screen print my custom t-shirts?', a: 'Compare both methods for the same garment, artwork, placement, quantity, feel, care, deadline, and current price. The production partner should document compatibility and quote each suitable option.' },
 { q: 'What\'s the best t-shirt for embroidery?', a: 'There is no universal best t-shirt. Compare exact products such as the Carhartt K87, Bayside 5100, and Hanes Beefy-T by fabric, fit, care, availability, price, and decoration compatibility.' },
 { q: 'Will embroidered t-shirts pucker over time?', a: 'Puckering risk depends on the exact fabric, fit, artwork, stitch density, backing, use, laundering, and care. Review a proof or sample when appropriate. Follow the garment and decoration care instructions.' },
 { q: 'How does embroidered t-shirt cost compare to screen printed?', a: 'Commercial terms vary by garment, artwork, placement, colors, stitch count, quantity, partner, and deadline. Compare current written quotes for the same order. Do not rely on a fixed quantity threshold.' },
 { q: 'Can you embroider a back design on a t-shirt?', a: 'Some products and designs may support back embroidery. Ask the production partner to compare compatible methods, comfort, stitch count, care, price, and timing for the exact garment and artwork.' },
 { q: 'Where can I get custom embroidered t-shirts in Las Vegas?', a: 'Bighorn Threads coordinates embroidery through selected production partners for Vegas contractors and service businesses. Carhartt K87, Bayside 5100, and Hanes Beefy-T are options to compare. Your quote confirms sizes, availability, and timing.' },
]

const schema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@graph': [
 { '@type': 'Article', headline: post.title, description: post.description, image: `https://bighornthreads.com${post.image}`, datePublished: post.isoDate, dateModified: '2026-08-21', author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/images/logos/bighorn-logo-color.png' } }, mainEntityOfPage: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` },
 { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/blog/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: post.title, item: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` }] },
 { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
 ],
}

const speakableSchema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@type': 'WebPage',
 url: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`,
 name: post.title,
 speakable: {
  '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification',
  cssSelector: ['h1', '.speakable-answer'],
 },
}
---

<BaseLayout title={post.title} description={post.description} canonical={`https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`} ogImage={post.image} type="article" publishedDate={post.isoDate}>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(speakableSchema)} />
 <article class="bg-concrete">
 <header class="border-b border-hairline bg-paper">
 <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-20 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 lg:px-8">
 <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-ash" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-700">Home</a><span class="px-2">/</span><a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-gold-700">Blog</a></nav>
 <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">{post.category}</span>
 <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{post.title}</h1>
 <p class="mb-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-ash">When embroidered tees are worth the cost, when to screen print instead, and which blanks take embroidery cleanly.</p>
 <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-hairline pt-6 font-mono text-sm text-ash"><span class="text-gold-600">Bighorn Threads Team</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span>{post.readTime}</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><time datetime={post.isoDate}>{post.date}</time></div>
 </div>
 </header>
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><img src={post.image} alt="Representative embroidered work tee for artwork and placement planning" width="1200" height="675" loading="eager" class="w-full border border-hairline object-cover" /></div>
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

 <aside class="mb-10 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7">
 <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">Quick Answer</p>
 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-xl speakable-answer">Choose embroidered or screen-printed t-shirts after reviewing the exact garment, artwork, placement, quantity, feel, care, availability, deadline, and current quote. The production partner must approve compatibility before production.</p>
 </aside>

 <h2 id="when-to-embroider" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">When Embroidered Tees Make Sense</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Embroidery may fit these program goals:</p>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Textured chest marks.</strong> Compare the appearance and feel of embroidery with other compatible methods on the exact garment.</li>
 <li><strong>Smaller programs.</strong> Compare current written quotes because minimums, setup, and per-piece pricing vary.</li>
 <li><strong>Service tech tees.</strong> A chest mark may support identification when it follows the employer's branding and dress policy.</li>
 <li><strong>Protective tees and base layers.</strong> The employer and current manufacturer documentation determine garment and decoration eligibility. Thread choice alone does not preserve a certification.</li>
 <li><strong>Tees with chest-only designs.</strong> When there's no need for a back logo or large design.</li>
 </ul>

 <h2 id="when-to-print" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">When Screen Printing Wins on Tees</h2>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Full-back designs.</strong> Ask the production partner to compare <a href="/services/screen-printing-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">screen printing</a> with other compatible methods.</li>
 <li><strong>Larger quantities.</strong> Compare current written quotes because setup, quantity breaks, and per-piece pricing vary by order.</li>
 <li><strong>Large bold designs.</strong> Block letters, simple shapes, oversized graphics print well and look intentional.</li>
 <li><strong>Multi-color complex designs.</strong> Ask the production partner to compare screen printing, DTF, and other compatible methods against the exact artwork and garment.</li>
 <li><strong>Field crew tees.</strong> Compare exact garments and decoration methods against abrasion, laundering, replacement policy, use, care, and budget.</li>
 </ul>

 <h2 id="best-blanks" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">T-Shirt Blanks to Compare for Embroidery</h2>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Carhartt K87 Workwear Pocket Tee</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Review current manufacturer data for fabric, construction, fit, pocket details, care, colors, sizes, and intended use. Confirm availability and decoration compatibility. See our <a href="/blog/carhartt-custom-embroidery-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">Carhartt custom embroidery</a> guide.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Bayside 5100 Heavyweight Tee</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Review current manufacturer data for fabric, construction, fit, care, country of origin, colors, and sizes. Confirm availability, decoration compatibility, price, and timing.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Hanes Beefy-T (5180)</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Review current manufacturer data for fabric, construction, fit, care, colors, and sizes. Compare availability, decoration compatibility, price, and timing with other exact products.</p>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Performance / Moisture-Wicking Tees</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Carhartt Force, Sport-Tek PosiCharge, and other performance tees may be options to compare. Review current manufacturer claims, decoration compatibility, dye-migration risk, use, care, availability, and price for the exact product.</p>

 <h2 id="placement" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Placement and Sizing</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Possible placements include the following. Final size, stitch count, backing, and placement depend on the exact garment and artwork.</p>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Left chest:</strong> A possible logo placement when the garment construction supports it.</li>
 <li><strong>Right chest:</strong> Employee name (for service tech roles)</li>
 <li><strong>Sleeve:</strong> Optional secondary mark</li>
 <li><strong>Back yoke:</strong> Possible but uncommon — embroidery scaled to a back logo gets expensive</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Avoid placements that put dense embroidery on stretchy fabric panels — sides, lower back — where pucker risk is higher.</p>

 <h2 id="costs" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">What Embroidered Tees Cost</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Pricing depends on the exact garment, artwork, placement, stitch count, colors, quantity, partner, and deadline. See <a href="/blog/how-much-to-embroider-a-shirt/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">how much it costs to embroider a shirt</a> for factors to confirm.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Minimums, setup charges, quantity breaks, product availability, and timing vary. Compare current written quotes for the exact order.</p>

 <div class="mt-12 border border-hairline bg-gold-500/5 p-7 sm:p-9">
 <h2 class="mb-3 font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Custom embroidered tees in Las Vegas</h2>
<p class="mb-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Bighorn Threads coordinates custom embroidered t-shirts through selected production partners. Your quote confirms exact products, availability, decoration terms, pricing, and timing.</p>
 <a href="/get-a-quote/" class="inline-flex min-h-[48px] items-center gap-2 bg-gold-500 px-7 py-3 text-base font-bold text-charcoal transition-all hover:bg-gold-600">Get a Quote →</a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
